*> Block entities, part 4: jukebox, lectern, bell, campfire, enchanting table, brushable block, beehive (docs/protocol/31-block-entities-4-jukebox-lectern-bell-campfire-brushable-beehive.md;
*> US12 phase 44). The data of the types lives in the BE-XI, BE-XT and BE-XF cells of the entity (roles in BESTATE.cpy). The programs are the rules of the sections;
*> what needs the world (the entity lists of the bell and the hive, the loot engine of the brush, item entities, sounds and particles) is done by the caller from their results.
*> Not here: the song data of the jukebox_song registry (the caller passes the song id, its length in ticks and its comparator output), the page count of a book (the caller passes
*> it to BE4-LECTERN-SET-BOOK and BE4-LECTERN-RESOLVE), the loot roll of a brush, the entity data of a stored bee beyond its id and HasNectar, the book model and the render pose
*> of the enchanting table (6.4 and 6.5), the jukebox's popOutTheItem offset (25 part 5).
*>
*>   BE4-REGISTRATION USING type, server ticker out, client ticker out       1.1 (1 jukebox, 2 bell, 3 campfire, 4 enchanting table client, 5 beehive server)
*>   BE4-DIR-INFO USING direction, 2D data value out, yRot out, clockwise out, step x, y, z out           1.3 (0 down, 1 up, 2 north, 3 south, 4 west, 5 east)
*>   BE4-CLOSER USING x, y, z (FLOAT-LONG), block x, y, z, d (FLOAT-LONG), result out; BE4-MTH-SIN / BE4-MTH-COS USING d, result (FLOAT-LONG)         1.3
*>   BE4-DROP-POS USING x, y, z, r1, r2, r3 (FLOAT-LONG), px, py, pz out; BE4-TRIANGLE USING c, d, a, b, result; BE4-DROP-SPLIT USING remaining, nextInt(21), chunk out
*>   Jukebox 2: BE4-SONG-TICKS, BE4-SONG-FINISHED, BE4-JUKEBOX-PLAY / -STOP / -TICK / -SET-ITEM / -RESUME / -SIGNAL / -RULES
*>   Lectern 3: BE4-LECTERN-SET-BOOK / -PAGE / -SIGNAL / -BUTTON / -RESOLVE / -USE-ITEM / -PLACEMENT / -DIRECT
*>   Bell 4: BE4-BELL-HIT / -EVENT / -REFRESH / -TICK / -COUNT / -COLOR / -PROPER / -RING / -NEIGHBOR / -ANIM
*>   Campfire 5: BE4-CAMPFIRE-RECIPE / -PLACE / -COOK / -COOLDOWN / -SMOKE / BE4-SMOKEY / BE4-CAMPFIRE-ITEMS
*>   Enchanting table 6: BE4-ENCH-TICK / BE4-ENCH-NAME. Brushable block 7: BE4-BRUSH / -RESET / -STATE / -DROP-POS / -TAG. Beehive 8: BE4-HIVE-* and BE4-IGNORED-TAG
*>   BE4-SAVE USING index, type, PB-BUFFER and BE4-LOAD-KEY USING index, name, tag, PB-BUFFER, handled out: the keys of these types (BEX-SAVE and BEX-LOAD-KEY of be-31-3.cob)

 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. BE4-REGISTRATION.
 DATA DIVISION.
 LINKAGE SECTION.
 01 L-TYPE                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-SERVER               BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-CLIENT               BINARY-LONG.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION USING L-TYPE L-SERVER L-CLIENT.
     MOVE 0 TO L-SERVER L-CLIENT
     EVALUATE L-TYPE
         WHEN 4
             MOVE 1 TO L-SERVER L-CLIENT
         WHEN 30
             MOVE 2 TO L-SERVER L-CLIENT
         WHEN 32
             MOVE 3 TO L-SERVER L-CLIENT
         WHEN 13
             MOVE 4 TO L-CLIENT
         WHEN 33
             MOVE 5 TO L-SERVER
     END-EVALUATE
     GOBACK.
 END PROGRAM BE4-REGISTRATION.

 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. BE4-DIR-INFO.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 01 WS-D2                  PIC X(6) VALUE "XX2013".
 01 WS-CW                  PIC X(6) VALUE "XX5342".
 01 WS-SX                  PIC X(6) VALUE "001001".
 LINKAGE SECTION.
 01 L-DIR                  BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-DATA                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-YROT                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-CW                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-SX                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-SY                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-SZ                   BINARY-LONG.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION USING L-DIR L-DATA L-YROT L-CW L-SX L-SY L-SZ.
     MOVE -1 TO L-DATA L-CW
     MOVE 0 TO L-SX L-SY L-SZ
     EVALUATE L-DIR
         WHEN 0
             MOVE -1 TO L-SY
         WHEN 1
             MOVE 1 TO L-SY
         WHEN 2
             MOVE 2 TO L-DATA
             MOVE 5 TO L-CW
             MOVE -1 TO L-SZ
         WHEN 3
             MOVE 0 TO L-DATA
             MOVE 4 TO L-CW
             MOVE 1 TO L-SZ
         WHEN 4
             MOVE 1 TO L-DATA
             MOVE 2 TO L-CW
             MOVE -1 TO L-SX
         WHEN OTHER
             MOVE 3 TO L-DATA
             MOVE 3 TO L-CW
             MOVE 1 TO L-SX
     END-EVALUATE
     COMPUTE L-YROT = FUNCTION MOD(L-DATA, 4) * 90
     GOBACK.
 END PROGRAM BE4-DIR-INFO.

